From: Patrick Quinn <patrick.jm.quinn@gmail.com>
Date: Sun, 18 Oct 2026 20:30:00 +0100
Subject: [PATCH] sailfishapp: tune the allocator on glibc only

Keel 0.1.0-35 calls mallopt(M_ARENA_MAX, M_TRIM_THRESHOLD,
M_MMAP_THRESHOLD) at launch and malloc_trim(0) after start-up. Both are
glibc extensions; musl has neither, so the build fails on Alpine.
musl's mallocng already returns freed pages to the kernel eagerly and
has no per-thread arenas, so there is nothing to tune: guard the calls
with __GLIBC__.
---
 sailfishapp/src/keellauncher.cpp | 2 ++
 sailfishapp/src/sailfishapp.cpp  | 6 +++++-
 2 files changed, 7 insertions(+), 1 deletion(-)

diff --git a/sailfishapp/src/keellauncher.cpp b/sailfishapp/src/keellauncher.cpp
--- a/sailfishapp/src/keellauncher.cpp
+++ b/sailfishapp/src/keellauncher.cpp
@@ -144,9 +144,11 @@
     // small limits hand it back (with trimMemory() after start-up): about
     // 1.5 MB less per app on an Xperia 10 II, as GLIBC_TUNABLES would,
     // which is read before any code of ours runs.
+#ifdef __GLIBC__
     mallopt(M_ARENA_MAX, 2);
     mallopt(M_TRIM_THRESHOLD, 128 * 1024);
     mallopt(M_MMAP_THRESHOLD, 128 * 1024);
+#endif
 
     // The Sailfish session sets QT_QPA_PLATFORM=wayland for its Qt 5 apps;
     // Keel wants Qt 6's EGL client explicitly. A value set on purpose for
diff --git a/sailfishapp/src/sailfishapp.cpp b/sailfishapp/src/sailfishapp.cpp
--- a/sailfishapp/src/sailfishapp.cpp
+++ b/sailfishapp/src/sailfishapp.cpp
@@ -221,7 +221,11 @@
     // Start-up's temporary allocations (QML compilation, image decoding)
     // are freed by now; give the pages back (keellauncher.cpp sets the
     // allocator's limits).
-    const auto trimMemory = []() { malloc_trim(0); };
+    const auto trimMemory = []() {
+#ifdef __GLIBC__
+        malloc_trim(0);
+#endif
+    };
     if (qEnvironmentVariableIsSet("KEEL_QML_WARMUP") && qEnvironmentVariableIntValue("KEEL_QML_WARMUP") == 0) {
         QTimer::singleShot(1500, view, trimMemory);
         return;
